  "term": "National Mental Health Association",
  "definition": "The National Mental Health Association was a voluntary U.S. organization focused on promoting mental health by supporting education and research in psychiatry. It developed from an earlier group founded in 1909 as the National Committee for Mental Hygiene and was linked with state and local mental health associations through charter and affiliation.",
